; Desktop Subsystem for Android (DSA)
; The guest Vulkan driver keeps a copy of each host-visible allocation an app maps and sends the
; host what the app wrote before each submit. It asks the kernel which pages those are: it write
; protects its copies with a userfaultfd of its own process (asynchronous mode, which needs no
; thread to answer faults), and at each submit lists the written pages and protects them again
; with the PAGEMAP_SCAN ioctl (0x6610, 'f' 16) on the process's own /proc/self/pagemap. Without
; them it hashes all of the app's mapped memory at every submit.
;
; The platform lets apps and system_server make a userfaultfd of their own (ART's garbage
; collector uses one), so creating one and its ioctls need no rule here. It lets a domain use
; only FIOCLEX and FIONCLEX on its own /proc files, though, so PAGEMAP_SCAN was refused. These
; rules allow that one ioctl, on the domain's own files only (self), for the domains that load
; the driver and may use a userfaultfd. The kernel lets a process scan another's pagemap only
; where it could trace it, and the driver only ever opens its own.
(allowx appdomain self (ioctl file (0x6610)))
(allowx system_server self (ioctl file (0x6610)))
